<title>GERMANY: MUNICH RE unlikely to increase capital in 1996/7.</title>
<headline>MUNICH RE unlikely to increase capital in 1996/7.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Muenchener Rueckversicherungs-AG, the world's largest reinsurance group, said on Monday it was unlikely that it would increase its capital in the 1996/97 business year.</p>
<p>Management board chairman Hans-Juergen Schinzler told a news conference that Munich Re increased its capital in November 1995 and had no pressing need for a further increase.</p>
<p>&quot;On balance I do not see a reason for a capital increase,&quot; Schinzler said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
